      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(opencode-go): remove deprecated mimo-v2-omni and mimo-v2-pro aliases",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenCode Go exposes `mimo-v2-omni` and `mimo-v2-pro` as supported models even though OpenCode marks both deprecated, omits them from the active Go documentation, and rejects agent requests for both routes.\n\nCloses #103311\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe OpenCode models endpoint still advertises compatibility rows for the deprecated aliases, but the upstream provider rejects requests to them. OpenClaw should keep the active product catalog bounded to callable current routes instead of masking the provider rejection. The two active V2.5 MiMo models (`mimo-v2.5` and `mimo-v2.5-pro`) are unaffected and continue to work.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers will no longer see `mimo-v2-omni` and `mimo-v2-pro` in the model catalog, preventing immediate provider errors when selecting these deprecated routes. The active MiMo V2.5 and V2.5 Pro models remain available and unaffected.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Removed `mimo-v2-omni` and `mimo-v2-pro` from `OPENCODE_GO_MODELS` array\n- Updated test model count assertion (20 -> 18)\n- OpenCode Go documentation confirms only V2.5 MiMo models are active",
